            {
              "id": "art-body",
              "type": "column",
              "props": {
                "span": 9
              },
              "children": [
                {
                  "id": "lede",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "For Florida fleets, staying competitive isn't just about drivers and contracts; it's about the equipment behind every haul. Buying new trailers outright may not always be the most cost-effective solution. Cash flow is tighter, freight demands shift, and downtime costs more than ever. That's why trailer leasing has become one of the most popular strategies for owner-operators and fleet managers looking to stay scalable without heavy upfront investments.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full",
                    "anchor": "post-lede"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-intro-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Leasing isn't just about lowering payments; it's about keeping fleets flexible, efficient, and prepared for the unexpected. Let's explore the best trailer leasing options for your business.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-benefits",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "The Benefits of Trailer Leasing",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "benefits"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-benefits-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Leasing provides fleets with the right balance of control and flexibility. Some of the biggest advantages include:",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "checks-benefits-2",
                  "type": "check-list",
                  "props": {
                    "mark": "dot",
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "text": "Lower upfront costs — no down payments or drained reserves, keeping capital free for fuel, payroll, and maintenance"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Predictable monthly expenses for easier budgeting at any fleet size"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Access to newer equipment, reducing repair headaches and downtime"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Scalability to add trailers during peak seasons and return them when demand slows"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "actions-benefits-3",
                  "type": "buttons",
                  "props": {
                    "align": "left",
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "ctaId": "browse-trailer-rentals",
                        "label": "Browse Rental Trailers",
                        "style": "primary"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-buy-vs-lease",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Trailer Leasing vs. Buying: What Florida Fleets Should Know",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "buy-vs-lease"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-buy-vs-lease-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Deciding between buying and leasing comes down to your goals and budget:",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "cards-buy-vs-lease-2",
                  "type": "card-lists",
                  "props": {
                    "variant": "type",
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "title": "Buying",
                        "points": [],
                        "intro": "This option may make sense if you plan to keep trailers for their full lifecycle, want complete ownership, and have capital available. Owning a trailer through financing can also offer potential tax advantages, such as the ability to claim depreciation or deduct interest expenses. Every situation is unique, so always consult a qualified tax professional for personalized advice."
                      },
                      {
                        "title": "Leasing",
                        "points": [],
                        "intro": "Leasing fits better if you want to avoid large upfront costs, rotate equipment regularly, and reduce depreciation. For many small to mid-size fleets, leasing provides the breathing room needed to stay profitable while keeping equipment modern and reliable."
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-types",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Types of Trailer Leasing Options",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "types"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-types-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Every fleet is different, so trailer leasing isn't one-size-fits-all. Here are some options you can expect:",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "cards-types-2",
                  "type": "card-lists",
                  "props": {
                    "variant": "type3",
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "title": "Short-Term Leasing",
                        "points": [],
                        "intro": "Ideal for seasonal peaks, project-specific hauls, or contract pilots. Short-term trailer leasing ensures you're not locked into long commitments for temporary needs."
                      },
                      {
                        "title": "Long-Term Leasing",
                        "points": [],
                        "intro": "Best for fleets that need predictable monthly costs without the hassle of ownership. Long-term leasing provides stability and helps manage total cost of ownership."
                      },
                      {
                        "title": "Specialized Equipment Leasing",
                        "points": [],
                        "intro": "From reefers to flatbeds, specialized trailers often come with higher price tags. Leasing helps spread out costs while still giving fleets access to the right tools for the job."
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-types-3",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "At Sun State Trailers, we can lease from one day to ten years, with lease options to own as well. It's all about working with you to find the right timeline.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "fig-1",
                  "type": "image",
                  "props": {
                    "width": "full",
                    "image": {
                      "src": "/img/blog/best-trailer-leasing-options-in-florida/1.jpg",
                      "width": 1280,
                      "height": 853,
                      "alt": "Sun State technician inspecting the interior of a trailer with a clipboard"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-uptime",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "How Trailer Leasing Supports Fleet Uptime",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "uptime"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-uptime-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Fleet managers know that downtime is the enemy of profitability. Leasing helps reduce downtime in a couple of ways:",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "list-uptime-2",
                  "type": "prose-list",
                  "props": {
                    "ordered": false,
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "text": "<strong>Newer trailers, fewer breakdowns</strong> — leased trailers are often newer, meaning fewer costly shop days"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "<strong>Maintenance programs</strong> — some leasing agreements offer a maintenance service as an add-on, saving both time and money"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-uptime-3",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Non-fuel operating costs remain at historic highs industry-wide, meaning every day a trailer sits idle eats into margins. Leasing helps fleets keep loads moving and revenue steady, even when other equipment is down for repairs.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-mixed-strategy",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Leasing as Part of a Mixed Strategy",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "mixed-strategy"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-mixed-strategy-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Leasing doesn't have to replace ownership; it can complement it. Many Florida fleets build a mixed strategy:",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "list-mixed-strategy-2",
                  "type": "prose-list",
                  "props": {
                    "ordered": false,
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "text": "Own a core set of trailers for stability"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Lease additional trailers for seasonal surges or new contracts"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Rent trailers for emergency coverage or unexpected breakdowns"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-mixed-strategy-3",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "This approach helps balance cost savings with flexibility while keeping service levels consistent for shippers.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "actions-mixed-strategy-4",
                  "type": "buttons",
                  "props": {
                    "align": "left",
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "ctaId": "browse-trailer-rentals",
                        "label": "Check Out Our Trailer Rentals",
                        "style": "primary"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-why-sunstate",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Why Choose Sun State Trailers for Semi-Trailer Leasing?",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "why-sunstate"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-why-sunstate-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Choosing the right leasing partner matters as much as the equipment itself. Sun State Trailers is Florida-based and customer-focused. Our leasing options are designed around your needs, not a cookie-cutter contract.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-why-sunstate-2",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "<strong>Here's what you can expect:</strong>",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "list-why-sunstate-3",
                  "type": "prose-list",
                  "props": {
                    "ordered": false,
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "text": "Straightforward terms — clear agreements without hidden surprises"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Local support — our Florida team is here when you need answers or repairs fast, with mobile trailer technicians"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Fleet-ready inventory — from dry vans to reefers, we maintain trailers that meet real operational demands"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "A long-term partner — we focus on relationships, not just transactions"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-why-sunstate-4",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "We understand that every fleet decision comes down to trust, ROI, and dependability. Our team works directly with you to ensure leasing is not just affordable but also practical for your business model.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-why-sunstate-5",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "For Florida fleets looking to maximize uptime, manage costs, and stay competitive, trailer leasing is one of the most effective strategies available. It gives you the flexibility to scale up or down without financial strain, access to newer trailers that reduce downtime, and the breathing room to focus on what matters most: delivering loads on time.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-why-sunstate-6",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "With <a href=\"/locations/trailer-sales\">Sun State Trailers</a>, you'll have a partner who values professionalism, dependability, and community. Whether you're exploring leasing, considering used trailers, or looking for short-term rentals, we'll help you find the right fit for your fleet.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "actions-why-sunstate-7",
                  "type": "buttons",
                  "props": {
                    "align": "left",
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "ctaId": "browse-trailer-rentals",
                        "label": "Secure Capacity Fast With Trailer Rentals",
                        "style": "primary"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
